## 10. Security and authority model

The OS needs explicit separation between capability and authority.

| Actor              | Allowed operations                        |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |
| Human Creator      | Full creative authority                   |
| Human Curator      | Editorial decisions within assigned scope |
| Human Auditor      | Evidence and forensic verification        |
| AI Generator       | Draft creation only                       |
| AI Analyzer        | Analytical reports only                   |
| Production Adapter | Import and asset registration             |
| Governor Engine    | Deterministic policy enforcement          |
| Master Player      | Playback of authorized releases           |

An AI system may recommend approval, but cannot generate an authenticated human approval.

Likewise, an administrator's technical ability to access data must not automatically grant creative release authority.

