I recommend carrying these principles into the final Android implementation as enforceable invariants.

1. Human Sovereignty: Human creator retains final creative authority.
2. Evidence Immutability: Historical evidence cannot be overwritten.
3. Mandatory Governance: Production cannot bypass required gates.
4. Layer Monotonicity: Higher layers cannot rewrite lower-layer evidence.
5. Provenance Continuity: Every derived artifact references its origin.
6. Decision Accountability: Every approval has an identifiable human authority.
7. Veto Supremacy: Human rejection blocks progression.
8. No Synthetic Authority: AI cannot impersonate human approval.
9. Release Exclusivity: Only G5-authorized packages enter the Master Player.
10. Version Integrity: Every material change creates a new revision.
11. Deterministic Governance: Identical inputs and policies produce reproducible evaluations.
12. Recovery Integrity: Restoring a project must not fabricate historical approvals.
13. Separation of Duties: Analysis, approval and release authorization remain distinct.
14. Constitutional Supremacy: No module can override these laws.

